 # Hybrid KV Cache Groups
+
+## Ordinary store lifetime candidate
+
+All chunks submitted for one request retain their own completion future and
+producer event; a later chunk does not replace an earlier remote reader.
+Normal and lazy offload report the request complete only after every chunk's
+device-aware future finishes. Preemption drains the same futures before a
+forward can reuse the source pages. Submission errors and lost server health
+with admitted stores raise without releasing events or reporting completion.
+This stops the engine; it does not implement transparent server recovery or
+the transfer-context close and re-registration protocol.
 
 ## Summary
 
